when u pass object java internally call valueOf --> calling obj.toString() method ---> if class does not contain toString() then go to hashCode-> print

Actually a.toString()  it will check does a means particular class contain toString() if not contain then print
com.kunal.staticExample.InnerClasses$Test@6acbcfc0


This is the default implementation of toString() from the Object class.

Breaking it down:
com.kunal.staticExample.InnerClasses$Test

This is the fully qualified class name (package + class name).
InnerClasses$Test means Test is a nested class inside InnerClasses. The $ indicates that Test is an inner class of InnerClasses.
@6acbcfc0

This is the hashcode of the object, represented in hexadecimal format (base 16).
It is generated by the hashCode() method of Object, which typically represents the object's memory address (though it's not guaranteed).

